# zmk-driver-pim447/Kconfig
# Top-level Kconfig for the PIM447 trackball driver module.

menuconfig PIM447
    bool "Pimoroni PIM447 trackball driver"
    depends on I2C
    depends on INPUT
    help
      Enable the Pimoroni PIM447 Trackball Breakout driver.

      The PIM447 is an I2C RGBW-illuminated clickable trackball using an
      onboard Nuvoton MCU to read 4 Hall-effect sensors and a dome switch.

if PIM447

module = PIM447
module-str = pim447
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

config PIM447_STATUS_INDICATOR
    bool "Use PIM447 LED as a system status indicator"
    depends on ZMK_BATTERY_REPORTING
    default n
    help
      When enabled, the PIM447's onboard RGBW LED reflects system state:
      dim white when idle, orange when battery is low, blinking red when
      battery is critical. The trackball's movement functionality is
      unaffected.

      Phase 1 (current): peripheral-local battery level only.
      Phase 2 (future): BLE host state, caps lock, layer indicators.

endif # PIM447
